  "solution": {
    "approach": "The approach to solve this problem is to use the properties of a binary tree. In a binary tree, the number of matches required to determine the winner is equal to the number of nodes minus one.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", n - 1);\n    return 0;\n}",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\nint main() {\n    int n;\n    std::cin >> n;\n    std::cout << n - 1 << std::endl;\n    return 0;\n}",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = scanner.nextInt();\n        System.out.println(n - 1);\n    }\n}",
      "Python3": "n = int(input())\nprint(n - 1)",
      "JavaScript": "const readline = require('readline');\nconst rl = readline.createInterface({\n    input: process.stdin,\n    output: process.stdout\n});\nrl.on('line', (input) => {\n    const n = parseInt(input);\n    console.log(n - 1);\n    rl.close();\n});"
    },
